  "body": "## What changed\n\n`app pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (heavy lane) re-pinned to platform-robust facts. Test-only; no product code.\n\n**Root cause, two parts (measured on macOS Apple silicon, release):**\n\n1. **Platform float.** On the same commit ecb54b7f, macOS plans the bore as 5786 moves / 5753 planar / 651 arcs (Z 20.000 alone on the rings, crossing at -2.33, -2.78), against the Windows measure of #850 / PR #865 (5530 / 5497 / 600). macOS is deterministic run to run, so this is not hash order. Rust does not fuse to FMA unasked, so the most likely source is platform libm last-place rounding (sin, cos, atan2, hypot) under the STEP tessellation and the planner, amplified by the planner's knife edges (#882, #982). The test was red on macOS from the moment the counts were pinned (6c198278). Filed as #1010 (effort:max).\n2. **Input change.** `git bisect --first-parent` ecb54b7f..f490458a on macOS puts the second rings level (Z 10.000, \"crosses itself\") at the #689 merge 575f02d8 (STEP chord cap + arc fit). #689 changed the bore's mesh and arcs on every platform (macOS now 6503 / 6467 / 222) and the heavy bore test was not re-measured there.\n\nNot a planner bug to fix narrowly: the crossing is caught by the planner's own guard and the level falls back to Offset rings by name, and the path verifies clean. Making the plan robust to sub-micron perturbation is #882 / #982 work.\n\n**Kept (unchanged):** no verifier warning (verifies clean), no planning-budget refusal, every rings level named by Z in the notes and the status line.\n\n**Replaced:** \"exactly one rings level, Z 20.000\" -> Z 20.000 is among the rings levels, every rings level is for a crossing, at most two of five levels on the rings; \"(5530, 5497, 600)\" -> arcs posted, 5000..=8000 moves, >= 98 % planar feeds. Decision: `docs/decisions/984-bore-heavy-pins.md`.\n\n## How tested (macOS Apple silicon, local, RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache)\n\n- Reproduced red on upstream/main f490458a (Z 20.000 and Z 10.000 crossings).\n- Bisect builds: ecb54b7f, 45e99d3e, 733409bf, 3bd54fc9 -> Z 20.000 only, 5786/5753/651; 575f02d8, bdf17d8a, f490458a -> Z 20.000 + Z 10.000.\n- Pinned: `app pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (release, --ignored): ok, 151 s.\n- app `pocket3d_hsm` (debug default): ok. motion `adaptive_band`, `adaptive_hsm`, `pocket3d_hsm` (debug): ok. motion `adaptive_hsm --ignored` (release): ok, 48 s.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nWindows and Linux: not run here. The band and level facts cover the Windows measure (5530, Z 20.000 alone) from before #689; the post-#689 Windows numbers are unknown.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\nfork synced at v0.17.0\n\nFixes #984\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
